            - Applied: notebook Loop A now plots Wilson 95% CI bands around both F and B rate curves (and the matched-rule panel), Loop E prints per-bin Wilson 95% CIs alongside the rates, Loop C cost helper documents binomial SE in a comment, chapter Loop C carries an SE note, and chapter Loop E reports Wilson CIs for the upper-tail bin.
        - Effect-weighted utility (medium) [APPLIED]
            - Current cost = c1 * P(false ship) + c2 * P(missed real win), constant per decision. In practice a missed +2pp win is worth ten times a missed +0.2pp win, and shipping a +0pp change costs little.
            - Add a Loop C variant: cost = c1 * E[max(0, -true_diff) | shipped] + c2 * E[max(0, true_diff - MMU) | not shipped], or equivalently sum the effect-weighted regret. Keep the constant-cost panel for intuition; show the effect-weighted panel alongside. Reject going further (full business model with revenue per user, time horizons, ramp-up curves) - out of scope for this capstone.
            - Applied: chapter Loop C carries a "Caveat: constant-per-decision cost" paragraph spelling out the issue and naming the effect-weighted formula. Notebook adds an `effect_weighted_cost` helper and a second sweep alongside the constant-cost sweep so the reader can compare both. Full business-model treatment deferred per scope.
